# Rank 1523 / CVE-2021-39181: OpenOLAT handed out XStream instances
# with no type restrictions, so deserializing a crafted XML file
# instantiated arbitrary classes (unsafe deserialization to remote
# code execution, CWE-502/CWE-94; OO-5548). createXStreamInstance in
# src/main/java/org/olat/core/util/xml/XStreamHelper.java did `return
# new EnhancedXStream(false);` -- no setupDefaultSecurity, no
# allowTypes -- and the module's other streams build the same
# way (some callers called XStream.setupDefaultSecurity ad hoc, the
# factory itself never did). the fixing commit is the fixing change
# (confirmed, "OO-5548: setup security of XStream by default", 73
# files): the factory now runs `XStream.setupDefaultSecurity(xstream)`
# before returning, a new allowDefaultPackage(xstream) helper applies
# allowTypesByWildcard(DEFAULT_PACKAGES) for the project's own
# packages, and every manager stream is audited to permissions or
# aliases. .
#
# ATTENTION, factory-shaped deserialization. The corpus HAS an
# XStream presence rule -- VYQL-DESER-007 (binding
# unrestrictedRequestParamDeserialization138, java/m420f6b67.vyql:
# 730) -- but its shape requires the factory to call
# registerConverter, which OpenOLAT's bare factory never does
# (converters register on the EnhancedXStream superclass or at call
# sites), so the rule cannot fire here; what is missing is the
# observation "an XStream instance is returned from a factory
# without any addPermission/setupDefaultSecurity" -- the
# converter-condition excludes exactly the bare-factory form this
# CVE shipped. Measured on the real code: scanning XStreamHelper.java
# reports zero findings at both revisions. A binding on OpenOLAT's
# own factory would detect this application rather than the
# weakness. No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry (loosening the presence rule's
# converter condition is a measured design decision, not a missing
# construct). No definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1523
# records the bare factory and the setupDefaultSecurity form, both
# asserting reject VYQL-DESER-007: when the factory observation
# lands, the bare form must flip to expect.

test "rank1523: the factory returns an unrestricted stream"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/org/olat/core/util/xml/XStreamHelper.java
  reject VYQL-DESER-007
  code
  ```
  package org.olat.core.util.xml;

  import com.thoughtworks.xstream.XStream;

  public class XStreamHelper {

      public static XStream createXStreamInstance() {
          return new EnhancedXStream(false);
      }

      public static XStream createXStreamInstanceForDBObjects() {
          return new EnhancedXStream(true);
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1523: the fixed revision locks the factory to default security"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/org/olat/core/util/xml/XStreamHelper.java
  reject VYQL-DESER-007
  code
  ```
  package org.olat.core.util.xml;

  import com.thoughtworks.xstream.XStream;

  public class XStreamHelper {

      public static final String[] DEFAULT_PACKAGES = new String[] { "org.olat.**" };

      public static final void allowDefaultPackage(XStream xstream) {
          xstream.allowTypesByWildcard(DEFAULT_PACKAGES);
      }

      public static XStream createXStreamInstance() {
          XStream xstream = new EnhancedXStream(false);
          XStream.setupDefaultSecurity(xstream);
          return xstream;
      }

      public static XStream createXStreamInstanceForDBObjects() {
          XStream xstream = new EnhancedXStream(true);
          XStream.setupDefaultSecurity(xstream);
          return xstream;
      }
  }
  ```
